{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011ChK5U5gtGDxXh3oxY7otr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`saveAll` now waits for every write before it resolves, and it rejects if any write fails.\n\n**The bug:** `items.forEach(async ...)` discards the promises from each async callback. The function then returned `items.length` straight away, so callers could resolve before any `db.put` had finished. A failing `put` also became an unhandled rejection instead of rejecting `saveAll`.\n\n**The fix** (`store.js:3-6`):\n\n```js\nasync function saveAll(items, db) {\n  await Promise.all(items.map((item) => db.put(item.id, item)));\n  return items.length;\n}\n```\n\nThe existing test passes: `node --test test/store.test.js` reports 1 pass, 0 fail. My first attempt, `node --test test/`, failed because Node tried to load the directory as a test file, not because of the fix.\n\nThe existing test would still pass with the old code, so it doesn't catch this bug. A useful addition would be a `db.put` that delays before storing, checking that `saveAll` doesn't resolve until the item is stored, plus a case where `put` rejects. I haven't added those; say if you want them."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":405,"cache_read_input_tokens":24828,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":405},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8dec9f7a-716f-40df-afd7-841a537068dd","uuid":"c883e265-0cbf-4f55-af8e-27639c41ac01","timestamp":"2026-11-23T02:33:39.141Z","request_id":"req_011ChK5U5XxDBwHNrw8X2TKx"}
